~ start
Book: A new day has started.
%19 Book: You get the choice to send somebody on an expedition. Which kind of expedition do you want to do?
% 
	Book: You had to stay at home because of a storm.
	=> END
%3
	Book: There is a sabretooth at your front door.
	=> sabretooth
	
	
	
	
	
	
	~ sabretooth
	- Attack him with a Spear
	if Global.spear >= 1
		Book: You successfully protected the cave and made him run away. Your spear broke during the fight.
		do Global.spear -= 1
		=> END
	else
		Book: You did not have a spear.
		
		% 
			Book: He did not seem to be bothered by you and he walked away.
		% 
			Book: You could not defend yourself against him, unaliving everyone.
			do Global.is_run_over = true
		=> END

- hunting expedition
	Book: You found a mammoth
	
	- Chase it
		%5
			Book: You got 20 Meat and 10 leather.
			do Global.meat += 20
			do Global.leather += 10
		%5
			Book: You injured yourself, but got 10 leather and 20 Meat.
			do Global.meat += 20
			do Global.leather += 10
			# do injure
	- Dont chase it
		Book: It ran away.





- gathering expedition
	%
		Book: You found berries.
		=> berries
	%
		Book: You found some herbs.
		=> herbs
	%
		Book: You found some sharp stones.
		=> stones
	%
		Book: You found some big leaves. You take them and return home.
		=> leaves
	%
		Book: You didn't find anything and went back home empty-handed.
		=> END
	~ berries
	- take them
		%4 
			Book: You took the berries.
			do Global.berries += 10
		% Book: You took the berries, but you got injured in the process. 
		
	- let them be
		Book: You left the berries and venture home.
	=> END
	
	
	~ herbs
	- take them
		%4 
			Book: You took the herbs.
			do Global.herbs += 3
		% Book: You took the herbs, but you got injured in the process. 
		
	- let them be
		Book: You left the herbs and venture home.
	=> END
	
	
	~ stones
	- take them
		%4 
			Book: You took the stones.
			do Global.stone += 3
		% Book: You took the stones, but you got injured in the process. 
		
	- let them be
		Book: You left the stones and venture home.
	~ leaves

=> END